2. Vulkan Specification

   The descriptions of the Vulkan API in the documentation comments of the files in
   crates/vulkan/src/vk/generated/ and in the file
   crates/vulkan-registry/vulkan-docs.json are excerpts from the sources of the Vulkan
   Specification, Khronos Vulkan-Docs (https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Docs), at
   the commit that crates/vulkan-registry/vulkan-docs.json records as "commit".

   Copyright 2014-2026 The Khronos Group Inc. and the other copyright holders that the
   source files of Vulkan-Docs name.
   SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0

   The excerpts are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
   License, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. A copy of the license is in
   LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt. The license disclaims warranties and limits liability.

   Changes made to the material: the short description of each reference page and the
   descriptions of structure members, command parameters and enumerants were selected;
   text that depends on API versions and extensions was resolved for all versions and all
   extensions of Vulkan. vulkan-docs.json holds the excerpts in their AsciiDoc form. In the
   documentation comments the AsciiDoc markup is converted to Markdown, references to the
   API link to the Rust items, references to other parts of the Specification are reduced
   to their text, and lines are wrapped anew.

   The excerpts are not the Vulkan Specification. The Specification that Khronos publishes
   at https://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/ is the normative text.

